description:
pkix-lint/src/lib.rs:1300-1336 builds `HashMap<&'static str, Option<Box<dyn Lint>>>` keyed by lint id, then on each `id` in the input slice does:

```rust
let key = by_id
    .keys()
    .copied()
    .find(|k| *k == id.as_str())
    .ok_or_else(...)?;
if let Some(lint) = by_id.get_mut(key).and_then(|slot| slot.take()) { ... }
```

The `keys().find()` walk is O(n) per lookup, making the whole loop O(n²) — exactly what the HashMap was meant to avoid. The roundabout shape exists because the author thought there was a lifetime issue between the runtime `id: String` and the `&'static str` keys.

There is no lifetime issue: `HashMap<&'static str, V>: HashMap<K, V>` where `K: Borrow<str>`, so `by_id.remove(id.as_str())` works directly and returns `Option<Option<Box<dyn Lint>>>`. The `Option<Box<dyn Lint>>` wrapper for tombstoning is also unnecessary — `HashMap::remove` already consumes the entry exactly once, which is the same single-take semantic the tombstone provides.

Idiomatic shape:

```rust
let mut by_id: HashMap<&'static str, Box<dyn Lint>> = self.lints.into_iter().map(|l| (l.id(), l)).collect();
let mut filtered = Vec::with_capacity(ids.len());
for id in ids {
    let lint = by_id.remove(id.as_str())
        .ok_or_else(|| ParseError::UnknownLintId { id: id.clone() })?;
    filtered.push(lint);
}
```

This is correctness-flavored (the O(n²) shape is wrong for the same reason the EvidenceIndex::build O(N²) was wrong in PKIX-7f92.11) and idiom-flavored (using HashMap correctly). Filed as P2 because typical lint counts are small (~50) so the practical penalty is microseconds, but the code reads as if the author lost a fight with the borrow checker — which is the canonical 'gave up on the borrow checker' smell from the ownership subsection.
